---
import LegalLayout from '../../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Trademark policy"
  description="When and how you can use the Klyna name and mark."
  heading="Trademark policy"
>
  <p>
    "Klyna" and the violet K mark are unregistered trademarks of the studio. We want you to be
    able to say "this works with Klyna" without asking us first; we just don't want anyone to
    pass off another product as Klyna or claim we endorse them when we don't.
  </p>

  <h2>You can, without asking:</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Write factual statements: "Built with Klyna", "Works with the Klyna WordPress plugin",
      "Klyna user since 2026".
    </li>
    <li>Use a small "Works with Klyna" badge in your footer, README, or app listing.</li>
    <li>Link to klyna.dev and use the wordmark in the link text.</li>
    <li>
      Quote screenshots of klyna.dev or our docs in articles, courses, and reviews, with credit.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Please don't, without asking:</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Name a product, plugin, theme, agency, or YouTube channel <em>Klyna-anything</em>
      (Klyna&nbsp;Pro, KlynaBoost, "by Klyna", etc.) if it isn't ours.
    </li>
    <li>
      Use the violet K mark as your own logo, app icon, or favicon.
    </li>
    <li>
      Imply endorsement, partnership, or certification we have not agreed to ("Official
      Klyna&nbsp;Partner", "Certified by Klyna").
    </li>
    <li>
      Register a domain that contains "klyna" as a meaningful part (klyna-seo.com,
      buyklyna.com, etc.).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>If you're not sure</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:hello@klyna.dev">hello@klyna.dev</a> with a sketch of what you want
    to do. We answer fast and we say yes more often than no.
  </p>

  <h2>"Works with Klyna" badge</h2>
  <p>
    A small SVG badge is available on <a href="/downloads">/downloads</a> under the "Brand"
    section. It is licensed for use only on sites that are actually running a Klyna tool.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
